The first statement retrieves interrupts that have been latched by KVM, but if this is not handled properly, it can lead to lost interrupts. The second statement attempts to get the current interrupt status from OPAL without first checking for KVM-latched interrupts, which can result in the CPU being stuck with an elevated CPPR if interrupts are not properly acknowledged.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
