if (opal_int_eoi((0x00 << 24) | XICS_IPI) > 0)
    force_external_irq_replay();
kvm_xirr = kvmppc_get_xics_latch();
```
Reason:
The first statement ensures that if an interrupt is acknowledged (EOI), it triggers a replay of external interrupts, which helps recover any interrupts snatched by KVM. The second statement is added to handle interrupts latched by KVM before querying OPAL, ensuring that all relevant interrupts are processed correctly and preventing the CPU from getting stuck in an elevated CPPR state.

